---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';

const title = 'Adaptive Lessons';
const description = 'Individualized music instruction for students with disabilities, medical conditions, or learning differences.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="content-page">
			<h1>Adaptive Lessons</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				For students with learning differences, disabilities, or medical conditions, we rebuild the
				lesson around the student — the instrument, the environment, the pacing, and the teaching
				method all flex to fit.
			</p>

			<h2>What changes</h2>
			<p>
				Instructors adjust instruction speed, expectations, and structure on a student-by-student
				basis — adding breaks, modifying instruments, and drawing on sensory-friendly strategies
				where needed. The goal extends past playing an instrument: sessions are also designed to
				build attention, memory, perception, cognitive flexibility, and emotional expression.
			</p>

			<h2>Who leads these lessons</h2>
			<p>
				Adaptive lessons are taught by board-certified music therapists trained to work across a
				wide range of disabilities and health needs, so instruction stays personalized rather than
				one-size-fits-all.
			</p>

			<h2>Areas of study</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Piano</li>
				<li>Guitar</li>
				<li>Voice</li>
				<li>Hand percussion</li>
				<li>Music theory, composition, and improvisation</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				Both studios are single-floor and wheelchair accessible, with wide doorways and accessible
				restrooms.
			</p>

			<div class="button-row">
				<a class="button" href="/free-trial">Book a Free Trial</a>
				<a class="button button-outline" href="/programs/music-therapy">See Music Therapy</a>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
